{"title":"Scholarships by State","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The following list of <b>State-specific scholarships</b> is primarily for students in the U.S. Some of these scholarships are subject-specific.\n</p><p>Also check out <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=National_scholarships\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"National scholarships\">National scholarships</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Alaska\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alaska</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Arizona\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Arizona</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Arkansas\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Arkansas</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#California\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">California</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Colorado\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Colorado</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#District_of_Columbia\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">District of Columbia</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Florida\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Florida</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Georgia\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Georgia</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Hawaii\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Hawaii</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Idaho\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Idaho</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Illinois\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Illinois</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Maine\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Maine</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Maryland\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Maryland</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Massachusetts\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Massachusetts</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Michigan\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Michigan</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Missouri\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Missouri</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Montana\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Montana</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Nevada\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Nevada</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#New_Mexico\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">New Mexico</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#New_York\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">New York</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#North_Dakota\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">North Dakota</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Oregon\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Oregon</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Pennsylvania\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">23</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Pennsylvania</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#South_Dakota\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">24</span> <span class=\"toctext\">South Dakota</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-25\"><a href=\"#Texas\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">25</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Texas</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-26\"><a href=\"#Utah\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">26</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Utah</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-27\"><a href=\"#Virginia\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">27</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Virginia</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-28\"><a href=\"#Washington\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">28</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Washington</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-29\"><a href=\"#Washington,_D.C.\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">29</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Washington, D.C.</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-30\"><a href=\"#Wyoming\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">30</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Wyoming</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-31\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">31</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alaska\">Alaska</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Alaska\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>New Alaska Scholarship Program - Alaska residents who will be attending school in Alaska are eligible. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://akadvantage.alaska.gov/Grants_and_Scholarships/Scholarships.aspx\">website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Arizona\">Arizona</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Arizona\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Arizona Commission for Postsecondary Education - <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.azhighered.org/\">website</a></li>\n<li>Arizona Community Foundation - <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.azfoundation.org/\">website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li>\n<li>Arizona Private School Association Scholarship Program - The Arizona Private School Association awards $1000 Scholarships to <b>every</b> public, private and charter High School in Arizona - <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.arizonapsa.org/scholarships.htm\">website</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Arkansas\">Arkansas</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Arkansas\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Arkansas Department of Higher Education <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.adhe.edu/divisions/financialaid/Pages/fa_programs.aspx\">website</a></li>\n<li>Governor's Scholars Program - awards substantial amounts of money to Arkansas students who stay in the state for college (based on ACT/SAT/PSAT scores) - <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.adhe.edu/divisions/financialaid/Pages/fa_govscholars.aspx\">website</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"California\">California</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: California\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Governor's Scholarship Programs for California <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.cagovernorsscholars.org/\">website</a> (NOTE: granted in 2000-2002)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (Los Angeles) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://publicaffairs.disneyland.com/education/youth-scholarships/youth_scholarships.html\">The Disneyland Resort Scholarship Program</a> for Orange County high school seniors who have demonstrated excellence in volunteerism and leadership.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.goodtidings.org/\">Good Tidings Foundation Community Service Scholarships</a> for high school seniors in the Greater Bay Area.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Colorado\">Colorado</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Colorado\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"District_of_Columbia\">District of Columbia</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: District of Columbia\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>See <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=D.C._Area_Scholarships\" title=\"D.C. Area Scholarships\">D.C. Area Scholarships</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (D.C.) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Florida\">Florida</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Florida\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (Miami) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Georgia\">Georgia</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Georgia\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (Atlanta) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Hawaii\">Hawaii</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Hawaii\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Idaho\">Idaho</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Idaho\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Illinois\">Illinois</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Illinois\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (Chicago) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jlrockford.org/scholarships.asp\">Junior League of Rockford Outstanding Volunteer Scholarship</a> for a high school senior in Winnebago County.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Maine\">Maine</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Maine\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.famemaine.com\">famemaine.com</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mainecf.org\">mainecf.org</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Society_of_Civil_Engineers_Maine_Section\" title=\"American Society of Civil Engineers Maine Section\">American Society of Civil Engineers Maine Section</a></li>\n<li>Barking Foundation Scholarship - These &lt;dollar/&gt;3,000 scholarships are available to any Maine resident seeking higher education. Financial need is considered. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.barkingfoundation.org\">website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maine_Business_%26_Prof._Women%27s_Club_-_Rachel_E._Lemieux_Youth_Scholarship\" title=\"Maine Business &amp; Prof. Women&#39;s Club - Rachel E. Lemieux Youth Scholarship\">Maine Business &amp; Prof. Women's Club - Rachel E. Lemieux Youth Scholarship</a></li>\n<li>Mainely Character Scholarship - <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mainelycharacter.org\">website</a></li>\n<li>Senator George J. Mitchell Scholarship - for seniors of Maine public schools for &lt;dollar/&gt;1,250 per year for up to four years. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mitchellinstitute.org/scholarships.html\">website</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Maryland\">Maryland</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Maryland\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>See <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=D.C._Area_Scholarships\" title=\"D.C. Area Scholarships\">D.C. Area Scholarships</a></li>\n<li>Maryland Distinguished Scholar Award for academic achievement or talent in the arts <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mhec.state.md.us/financialaid/programdescriptions/prog_ds.asp\">website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (D.C.) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Massachusetts\">Massachusetts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Massachusetts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (Boston) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Michigan\">Michigan</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Michigan\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.skandalaris.org/college-scholarship/index_html\">Skandalaris Family Foundation Scholarship</a>. &lt;dollar/&gt;2,000 scholarships for current undergraduate students and high school seniors.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Michigan_Council_of_Women_in_Technology_Scholarship&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Michigan Council of Women in Technology Scholarship (page does not exist)\">Michigan Council of Women in Technology Scholarship</a> for female students who are residents of Michigan. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mcwtf.org/Scholarships_149.html\">Website</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Missouri\">Missouri</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Missouri\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_James_L._and_Nellie_M._Westlake_Scholarship_Program\" title=\"The James L. and Nellie M. Westlake Scholarship Program\">The James L. and Nellie M. Westlake Scholarship Program</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Montana\">Montana</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Montana\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Siegel_Service_Technology_Scholarships&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Siegel Service Technology Scholarships (page does not exist)\">Siegel Service Technology Scholarships</a> for undergraduates in Montana.  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://students.sae.org/awdscholar/scholarships/siegel/\">Website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Nevada\">Nevada</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Nevada\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"New_Mexico\">New Mexico</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: New Mexico\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"New_York\">New York</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: New York\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Posse_Foundation_Scholarship\" title=\"Posse Foundation Scholarship\">Posse Foundation Scholarship</a> for students living in select cities (New York City) who show leadership and academic potential and are nominated by their high schools. Participating universities include Boston University, Pepperdine University, Pomona College, UC Berkeley, UCLA, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, University of Pennsylvania, University of Southern California, and many other schools as listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.possefoundation.org/our-university-partners/participating-schools/\">here</a>.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"North_Dakota\">North Dakota</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: North Dakota\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Oregon\">Oregon</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Oregon\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Pennsylvania\">Pennsylvania</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Pennsylvania\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>New Economy Technology Scholarship (NETS) for undergraduates studying in approved technology, science, or allied health fields who are Pennsylvania residents and students and willing to work full-time in Pennsylvania after graduation. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.pheaa.org/specialprograms/nets/New_Economy_Technology_Scholarship.shtml\">Website</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"South_Dakota\">South Dakota</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24\" title=\"Edit section: South Dakota\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Texas\">Texas</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: Texas\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.ozarkawater.com/WeCare/\">Every Drop Counts Earth Science Scholarship Fund</a> for Texas high school seniors pursuing degrees in earth/environmental sciences.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.youthlaunch.org/programs/scholarship.php\">YouthLaunch Scholarship for Outstanding Service</a>. A &lt;dollar/&gt;3,000 scholarship for Texas students who demonstrate commitment to their community service projects.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Utah\">Utah</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Scholarships_by_State&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26\" title=\"Edit section: Utah\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Western_Undergraduate_Exchange\" title=\"Western Undergraduate Exchange\">Western Undergraduate Exchange</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Virginia\">Virginia</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span 